The start-keycloak command provides a development environment for testing Keycloak themes by launching a Docker-based Keycloak instance with your theme mounted. This command handles Docker container setup, version selection, theme building, file watching, and optional Hot Module Replacement (HMR) for Single-Page Account and Admin themes.
For information about the build process itself, see build. For HMR implementation details, see Hot Module Replacement.
Sources: src/bin/start-keycloak/start-keycloak.ts40-857
The command is invoked via:
| Option | Type | Description | 
|---|---|---|
| --port | number | Port to expose Keycloak on (default: 8080) | 
| --keycloak-version | string | Specific Keycloak version tag (e.g., "26", "26.0.7") | 
| --realm-json-file-path | string | Path to custom realm configuration JSON | 
These options can also be configured in BuildContext.startKeycloakOptions via package.json or vite.config.ts.
