The command performs two critical checks before proceeding:
The command verifies Docker (or Podman) is installed by executing docker --version and checking for either "docker" or "podman" in the output.
Sources: src/bin/start-keycloak/start-keycloak.ts48-80
The command executes docker info to verify the Docker daemon is running. If this fails, the user is prompted to start Docker Desktop.
Sources: src/bin/start-keycloak/start-keycloak.ts82-104
The version selection logic has three paths:
Explicit CLI Version: If --keycloak-version is provided, it's validated against allSupportedTags from getSupportedDockerImageTags().
BuildContext Configuration: If buildContext.startKeycloakOptions.dockerImage.tag is set, that tag is used directly.
Interactive Selection: The user is prompted with latestMajorTags, with theme-type-specific filtering:
