Before starting the container, the command performs two sequential builds:
The appBuild() function parses package.json to find the build script and executes the pre-Keycloakify build steps (typically vite build or equivalent).
Sources: src/bin/start-keycloak/appBuild.ts20-231 src/bin/start-keycloak/start-keycloak.ts299-310
The keycloakifyBuild() function executes npx keycloakify build with the KEYCLOAKIFY_BUILD_FOR_KEYCLOAK_MAJOR_VERSION environment variable set to target the specific Keycloak major version.
Sources: src/bin/start-keycloak/keycloakifyBuild.ts15-43 src/bin/start-keycloak/start-keycloak.ts312-324
The system supports two types of extension JARs configured in BuildContext.startKeycloakOptions.extensionJars:
| Type | Description | Processing | 
|---|---|---|
| path | Local filesystem path | Verified with existsAsync() | 
| url | Remote URL | Downloaded via downloadAndExtractArchive() | 
For Keycloak versions >= 21, the keycloakify-logging-${VERSION}.jar extension is automatically included. This extension enables realm configuration persistence by emitting keycloakify-logging: REALM_CONFIG_CHANGED events.
