HMR is enabled when all of the following conditions are met:
NO_DEV_SERVER environment variable is not set to "true"When enabled, startViteDevServer() launches a Vite dev server on a random port and passes the port to the Docker container via the KEYCLOAKIFY_SPA_DEV_SERVER_PORT environment variable.
Sources: src/bin/start-keycloak/start-keycloak.ts469-520 src/bin/shared/constants.ts85
The Docker container mounts several critical volumes:
| Volume Type | Local Path | Container Path | Mode | 
|---|---|---|---|
| Theme JAR | {cacheDirPath}/{jarFilename} | /opt/keycloak/providers/keycloak-theme.jar | ro | 
| Extension JARs | {extensionJarPath} | /opt/keycloak/providers/{jarBasename} | ro | 
| Theme Directories | {keycloakifyBuildDirPath}/theme/{themeName} | /opt/keycloak/themes/{themeName} | rw | 
| Realm JSON | {realmJsonFilePath} | /opt/keycloak/data/import/{realmName}-realm.json | ro | 
Theme directories are mounted read-write (rw) to enable live updates during development.
Sources: src/bin/start-keycloak/start-keycloak.ts524-607
The image reference defaults to quay.io/keycloak/keycloak:{dockerImageTag} but can be customized via BuildContext.startKeycloakOptions.dockerImage.reference.
