The file watcher monitors the project for changes and triggers automatic rebuilds.
{projectDirPath}/src{publicDirPath}{projectDirPath}/package.json{projectDirPath}/vite.config.ts and vite.config.js{projectDirPath}/index.htmlsrc/ directory (for development on Keycloakify itself)When doStartDevServer is true, the following paths are ignored because they're covered by HMR:
{themeSrcDirPath}/account/**/* (Single-Page Account theme files){themeSrcDirPath}/admin/**/* (Admin theme files){themeSrcDirPath}/shared/@patternfly/**/*{themeSrcDirPath}/shared/keycloak-ui-shared/**/*Exception: .properties files always trigger a rebuild, even under HMR directories.
runExclusive.build() ensures only one rebuild runs at a timeappBuild() → keycloakifyBuild() → extractThemeResourcesFromJar()Sources: src/bin/start-keycloak/start-keycloak.ts720-856
Once the container is running, the command outputs connection information:
http://localhost:{port}{kcHttpRelativePath}
- user: admin
- password: admin
The kcHttpRelativePath is extracted from BuildContext.startKeycloakOptions.dockerExtraArgs if KC_HTTP_RELATIVE_PATH is specified.
The command generates a test URL based on TEST_APP_URL constant:
https://my-theme.keycloakify.dev?port={port}&kcHttpRelativePath={path}&realm={name}&client={name}
This URL points to a test application that integrates with the local Keycloak instance.
- username: {configuredUsername}
- password: password123
